            <ArticleTitle>[Early relaparotomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An analysis of 14565 operations on organs of the abdominal cavity has shown that main causes of early relaparotomies were peritonites (47,4%), intestinal obstruction (33,3%), eventration of the abdominal organs (16,0%) and hemoperitoneum (3,3%). The highest lethality was after postoperative peritonitis (54,1%). For the recent 10 years the total lethality has become 31,6% lower due to better diagnosis and early relaparotomies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
